                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Hebrew Letter Tet Stock Illustration - Download Image Now ...](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110523-2762-0139-0000-a63bc8445cdf:4)\nThe [Hebrew Letter Tet](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137081/jewish/Tet.htm) (ט) is the ninth letter of the Hebrew alphabet and has a numeric value of **9**.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137081/jewish/Tet.htm)\n\n### Key Characteristics\n\n- **Sound:** Pronounced like the \"t\" sound in \"take\" or \"get\".[[1]](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/1HwnNtqjYQU)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iFihW891s2Y&t=1)\n- **Ancient Meaning:** Originally represented a clay or wicker container, basket, or wheel used for storage.[[1]](https://hebrewtoday.com/alphabet/the-letter-tel-%D7%98/)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iFihW891s2Y&t=1)[[3]](https://www.ancient-hebrew.org/ancient-alphabet/tet.htm)\n- **Frequency:** It is the least frequently occurring letter in the Hebrew Bible (Torah).[[1]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Tet/tet.html)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/FxcxmH_Znok)\n- **Symbolism of 9:** Corresponds to the nine months of human gestation, symbolizing hidden goodness, preparation, and the birth of something new.[[1]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137081/jewish/Tet.htm)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g_cmVuxle00&t=6)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iFihW891s2Y&t=1)\n- **Meaning of Goodness:** It is the first letter of the word ***tov** * (טוב), which means \"good\". The shape of the letter is often described as inverted or coiled, symbolizing hidden or interior good (like a child in the womb).[[1]](https://inner.org/hebleter/tet.htm)[[2]](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/FxcxmH_Znok)[[3]](https://www.hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Tet/tet.html)\n\nWould you like to know more about its **gematria** (numerical value) or see examples of **Hebrew words** that start with Tet?",
